DjVu fragments
description: a page number and a rectangle in the page's native pixels
- >
  A **djvu fragment** is the DjVu twin of the [PDF fragment](*::annotations:fragments:pdf): a
  **page** (counted from 1) and a rectangle with `x`, `y` from the page's top-left corner - here in
  the page's **native raster pixels** (the decoded page image's own resolution), zoom-independent
  the same way:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  type: djvu
  page: 12
  x: 340
  y: 1210
  w: 620
  h: 140
- >
  The fragment also embeds a PNG crop of the region ([the crop sidecar](*::annotations:fragments:crop)).
